    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 1167,
   "fen": "rnbqk2r/ppp1ppbp/3p1np1/8/3PP3/2N1BP2/PPP3PP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Don't rush the queen to d2 — it allows the annoying knight to g4 hitting the bishop. So f3 first, ruling out that jump and preparing the queen move, since we're castling long anyway.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "f3 before Qd2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 1180.5,
   "fen": "rnbq1rk1/ppp1ppbp/3p1np1/8/3PP3/2N1BP2/PPPQ2PP/R3KBNR b KQ - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "O-O",
    "Qd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "The queen to d2 does two jobs: it readies queenside castling, and it sets up the bishop swinging to h6 to trade off his fianchettoed bishop.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "teaches": [
    "Qd2’s dual purpose"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 1185.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pppnppbp/3p1np1/8/3PP3/2N1BP2/PPPQ2PP/R3KBNR w KQ - 3 7",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 1195.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pppnppbp/3p1npB/8/3PP3/2N2P2/PPPQ2PP/R3KBNR b KQ - 4 7",
   "line": [
    "Bh6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Top priority is eliminating his strongest piece, the fianchetto bishop — and he correctly counters in the centre with c5.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "trade the fianchetto defender"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 1198.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp1nppbp/3p1npB/2p5/3PP3/2N2P2/PPPQ2PP/R3KBNR w KQ - 0 8",
